cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the associated study, please cite the paper below."
title: "PathwayMoE-Perturb: When does gene-regulatory structure help perturbation prediction?"
abstract: >-
  A leakage-audited, statistically rigorous controlled study of whether a
  gene-regulatory-network (GRN) inductive bias improves out-of-distribution
  single-cell perturbation prediction. The architecture is held fixed; only GRN
  quality (none / random / TRRUST curated / data-derived co-expression /
  co-response / ground-truth) and injection mechanism (hard attention mask vs
  soft message-passing) are varied. Evaluated on a 22.6M-cell Tahoe-100M subset
  and on synthetic data with known generative GRN. Headline result: no GRN
  prior significantly improves real-data OOD prediction.
type: software
